cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Coding Agent Role Boundary: A Corrected Pilot Study"
authors:
  - name: "Dev"
    alias: "Dev10-sys"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dev10-sys/coding-agent-role-boundary"
url: "https://github.com/Dev10-sys/coding-agent-role-boundary"
abstract: >
  A reproducible mechanistic interpretability pilot studying whether coding agents
  internally represent persistent repository instructions as higher-authority roles
  due to wording or presentation, even when the actual source is lower-trust workspace
  content. Includes a corrected probe design, a controlled warning-salience ablation,
  and a behavioral sandbox with actual tool-call execution.
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - prompt injection
  - role confusion
  - coding agents
  - AI safety
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-11"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Prompt Injection as Role Confusion"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12277"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/role-confusion/prompt-injection-as-role-confusion"
    notes: "Commit ec333c40fd43fe991e1ebf66765051b6d7e35784 used as reference"
